        "original_id": "123774d0-7640-50df-b7d7-94199f791546",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harvey Pekar, Denise Levertov, Joyce Brabner\n- Works: American Splendor, A Door in the Hive, August Houseplant\n- Roles: comic book writer, music critic, media personality, poet, political comics writer\n\nFacts:\n- Denise Levertov was born on 24 October 1923 and was an American poet.\n- Harvey Pekar was born on October 8, 1939 and became an American underground comic book writer, music critic, and media personality.\n- Joyce Brabner was born on March 1, 1952 and is a writer of political comics.\n- Denise Levertov wrote the collection A Door in the Hive, which includes the poem August Houseplant.\n- Harvey Pekar was best known for his autobiographical comic series American Splendor.\n- Joyce Brabner is the widow of Harvey Pekar.\n- Denise Levertov died on 20 December 1997.\n- Harvey Pekar died on July 12, 2010.",
